{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc | sed -n '389,855p'\"","aggregated_output":"   389\t(defn- absorb!\n   390\t  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n   391\t   id is outstanding is taken: a not-found error marks the reflection\n   392\t   gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's descriptor and\n   393\t   declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is emitted on the\n   394\t   event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is filed under its\n   395\t   id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose id is not\n   396\t   outstanding, and values that are not well-formed answers, are\n   397\t   dropped as diagnostics.\"\n   398\t  [link v]\n   399\t  (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n   400\t    (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n   401\t      (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   402\t        (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n   403\t              req (:req entry)\n   404\t              op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   405\t              e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n   406\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n   407\t          (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n   408\t          (cond\n   409\t            (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n   410\t            (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n   411\t                (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   412\t                          (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n   413\t                  (emit! link v)))\n   414\t\n   415\t            (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n   416\t            ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n   417\t            ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n   418\t            (when (nil? e)\n   419\t              (learn! refl v)\n   420\t              (emit! link v))\n   421\t\n   422\t            (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n   423\t            (emit! link v)\n   424\t\n   425\t            :else\n   426\t            (do (swap! link assoc-in\n   427\t                       [:filed id] {:req req :ans v :reflection refl})\n   428\t                (install-more! link v))))))))\n   429\t\n   430\t\n   431\t(defn- channel-loss!\n   432\t  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n   433\t   abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n   434\t   the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n   435\t   still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n   436\t  [link]\n   437\t  (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n   438\t    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   439\t      (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   440\t                   :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   441\t                   :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   442\t    (swap! (:reflection entry) update :ids disj id))\n   443\t  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n   444\t\n   445\t\n   446\t(defn- drain!\n   447\t  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n   448\t   caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n   449\t   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n   450\t   cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n   451\t   further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n   452\t   caller never asks it remotely -- so resend-after re-sends it.\"\n   453\t  [link]\n   454\t  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   455\t    (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\n   456\t      (when (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\n   457\t        (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n   458\t    (loop []\n   459\t      (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\n   460\t        (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   461\t          :dao.stream/ok\n   462\t          (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\n   463\t              (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   464\t              (recur))\n   465\t          :dao.stream/blocked nil\n   466\t          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\n   467\t          :dao.stream/gap\n   468\t          (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\n   469\t          nil)))))\n   470\t\n   471\t\n   472\t;; =============================================================================\n   473\t;; The reflection (2.4)\n   474\t;; =============================================================================\n   475\t\n   476\t(defn- result\n   477\t  [outcome]\n   478\t  {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\n   479\t\n   480\t\n   481\t(defn- refl-descriptor\n   482\t  \"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\n   483\t   with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\n   484\t   descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\n   485\t   descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\n   486\t   channel loss.\"\n   487\t  [refl]\n   488\t  (drain! (:link @refl))\n   489\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   490\t   :dao.stream/descriptor (:descriptor @refl)\n   491\t   :dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)})\n   492\t\n   493\t\n   494\t(defn- surface-lacks?\n   495\t  \"True when the source's declared surface is learned and lacks the\n   496\t   surface `op` needs. Before the probe's answer the reflection\n   497\t   declares #{:reader :writer :closable}, so every operation is\n   498\t   attempted; an operation the source turns out to lack is answered as\n   499\t   the no-surface case.\"\n   500\t  [refl op]\n   501\t  (let [s (:surface @refl)]\n   502\t    (and (some? s) (not (contains? s (required-surface op))))))\n   503\t\n   504\t\n   505\t(defn- filed-answer-outcome\n   506\t  \"The outcome a filed answer yields: a protocol error translated per\n   507\t   the rules, otherwise the source's outcome map verbatim.\"\n   508\t  [ans]\n   509\t  (or (some-> (:dao.stream.remote/error ans) translated)\n   510\t      (bare-outcome ans)))\n   511\t\n   512\t\n   513\t(defn- filed-cursor\n   514\t  \"A filed answer for anchor `a` sent by `refl`, returned without\n   515\t   being forgotten: minting is idempotent, so the answer stays as true\n   516\t   as when it was minted.\"\n   517\t  [link refl a]\n   518\t  (when-some [[_ entry] (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)]\n   519\t    (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))\n   520\t\n   521\t\n   522\t(defn- filed-next!\n   523\t  \"A filed answer for cursor `c` sent by `refl`: the outcome an\n   524\t   installed more element put at `c` for the stream `refl` serves,\n   525\t   else the filed answer of a next request for `c`; returned and\n   526\t   forgotten.\"\n   527\t  [link refl c]\n   528\t  (let [k [(:identity @refl) c]]\n   529\t    (or (when-some [o (get (:filed-cursors @link) k)]\n   530\t          (swap! link update :filed-cursors dissoc k)\n   531\t          (filed-answer-outcome o))\n   532\t        (when-some [[id entry]\n   533\t                    (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/next c)]\n   534\t          (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\n   535\t          (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))))\n   536\t\n   537\t\n   538\t(defn- retry-read\n   539\t  \"The answer a just-sent cursor request gives: the source's map,\n   540\t   invalid-anchor included, arrives later as an answer.\"\n   541\t  []\n   542\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n   543\t   :dao.stream/retry? true})\n   544\t\n   545\t\n   546\t(defn- send-or-count!\n   547\t  \"Send the request for `op` with `arg` when none of this reflection's\n   548\t   own is outstanding; otherwise count one further ask of the\n   549\t   outstanding request, which re-sends it at the link's resend-after\n   550\t   k.\"\n   551\t  [link refl op arg]\n   552\t  (if-some [id (outstanding-for link refl op arg)]\n   553\t    (count-ask! link id)\n   554\t    (send-request! link refl (wire-request link refl op [arg]))))\n   555\t\n   556\t\n   557\t(defn- refl-cursor\n   558\t  \"The cursor operation: a filed answer for the anchor is returned,\n   559\t   and a filed protocol error translated; otherwise a cursor request\n   560\t   is sent if none is outstanding, and the answer is transport-error\n   561\t   with :dao.stream/retry? true. Once closed, cursor answers closed;\n   562\t   once gone, transport-error naming not-found.\"\n   563\t  [refl a]\n   564\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\n   565\t    (drain! link)\n   566\t    (cond\n   567\t      (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\n   568\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n   569\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/cursor)\n   570\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n   571\t      :else\n   572\t      (or (filed-cursor link refl a)\n   573\t          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   574\t            (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)\n   575\t            (retry-read))\n   576\t          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n   577\t\n   578\t\n   579\t(defn- refl-next\n   580\t  \"The next operation: a filed answer for the cursor is returned and\n   581\t   forgotten; otherwise a next request is sent if none is outstanding,\n   582\t   and the answer is blocked -- nothing is observable at this position\n   583\t   through this handle yet. After close, filed outcomes then end. The\n   584\t   reflection never judges a cursor: cursor-mismatch and\n   585\t   invalid-cursor are only ever relayed from the source.\"\n   586\t  [refl c]\n   587\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\n   588\t    (drain! link)\n   589\t    (cond\n   590\t      (:closed? @refl)\n   591\t      (or (filed-next! link refl c) (result :dao.stream/end))\n   592\t\n   593\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n   594\t\n   595\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/next)\n   596\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n   597\t\n   598\t      :else\n   599\t      (or (filed-next! link refl c)\n   600\t          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n   601\t            (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/next c)\n   602\t            (result :dao.stream/blocked))\n   603\t          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n   604\t\n   605\t\n   606\t(defn- refl-append\n   607\t  \"The append! operation: send the request and return the channel\n   608\t   writer's outcome -- ok is acceptance on the outbound path, exactly\n   609\t   the contract's Writing rule for a transport that carries values\n   610\t   toward a stream elsewhere. The source's outcome is emitted on the\n   611\t   event writer when it is filed, correlated by id; append! never\n   612\t   answers the source's full. Only an accepted send is in flight: a\n   613\t   refused append! never crossed, so its effect is not unknown.\"\n   614\t  [refl v]\n   615\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\n   616\t    (drain! link)\n   617\t    (cond\n   618\t      (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\n   619\t      (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n   620\t      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/append!)\n   621\t      (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n   622\t      :else\n   623\t      (let [req (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/append! [v])\n   624\t            r (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)]\n   625\t        (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   626\t          (register! link refl req))\n   627\t        r))))\n   628\t\n   629\t\n   630\t(defn- refl-close\n   631\t  \"The close! operation, local: the reflection forgets its\n   632\t   outstanding ids, reporting each outstanding append! on the event\n   633\t   writer as append-unknown -- an append whose answer never arrives\n   634\t   has unknown effect; afterwards append! answers closed, cursor\n   635\t   answers closed, next answers filed outcomes then end, and nothing\n   636\t   crosses the wire. Idempotent, per the contract's Close.\"\n   637\t  [refl]\n   638\t  (let [link (:link @refl)]\n   639\t    (drain! link)\n   640\t    (when-not (:closed? @refl)\n   641\t      (doseq [id (:ids @refl)]\n   642\t        (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n   643\t          (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n   644\t            (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n   645\t                         :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n   646\t                         :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n   647\t          (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)))\n   648\t      (swap! refl assoc :closed? true :ids #{}))\n   649\t    (result :dao.stream/ok)))\n   650\t\n   651\t\n   652\t(deftype ReflectionHandle\n   653\t  [state]\n   654\t\n   655\t  stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   656\t\n   657\t  (descriptor\n   658\t    [_]\n   659\t    (refl-descriptor state))\n   660\t\n   661\t\n   662\t  stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   663\t\n   664\t  (cursor\n   665\t    [_ anchor]\n   666\t    (refl-cursor state anchor))\n   667\t\n   668\t\n   669\t  (next\n   670\t    [_ c]\n   671\t    (refl-next state c))\n   672\t\n   673\t\n   674\t  stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   675\t\n   676\t  (append!\n   677\t    [_ v]\n   678\t    (refl-append state v))\n   679\t\n   680\t\n   681\t  stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   682\t\n   683\t  (close!\n   684\t    [_]\n   685\t    (refl-close state)))\n   686\t\n   687\t\n   688\t;; =============================================================================\n   689\t;; The remote descriptor dispatch (2.2)\n   690\t;; =============================================================================\n   691\t\n   692\t(defn- valid-remote-descriptor?\n   693\t  \"A remote descriptor names a stream and a channel: the generic\n   694\t   envelope rules, the :dao.stream/remote type, and a channel\n   695\t   descriptor. It carries no authorization, no surface and no\n   696\t   anchors; the mirror answers those.\"\n   697\t  [d]\n   698\t  (and (stream/valid-descriptor? d)\n   699\t       (= :dao.stream/remote (:dao.stream/type d))\n   700\t       (contains? d :dao.stream/channel)))\n   701\t\n   702\t\n   703\t(defn attacher\n   704\t  \"The composition's :dao.stream/attach entry for :dao.stream/remote\n   705\t   descriptors; a dynamic dispatch table has this entry and no\n   706\t   :dao.stream/create one, because attaching through this transport\n   707\t   never creates. `opts` carries the composition data:\n   708\t   :dao.stream.remote/channels maps each channel descriptor this peer\n   709\t   reaches to its own end {:reader r :writer w} -- two ring buffers in\n   710\t   one process today, the ws, udp and pair channels of section 3\n   711\t   later; :dao.stream.remote/events is the optional event writer the\n   712\t   links emit on; :dao.stream.remote/resend-after is the links'\n   713\t   resend-after k, unbounded on an ordered reliable channel and small\n   714\t   on udp; :dao.stream.remote/budget is the budget stamped on every\n   715\t   next request. One link is kept per channel descriptor, shared by\n   716\t   every reflection through that channel. attach! answers ok at once\n   717\t   with a reflection handle and a local, opaque\n   718\t   :dao.stream/attachment -- the contract's deferred remote\n   719\t   confirmation -- and the link sends one descriptor probe for the\n   720\t   identity: its answer is the reflection's confirmation, not-found\n   721\t   marking the reflection gone, ok recording the source's descriptor\n   722\t   and declared surface.\"\n   723\t  [opts]\n   724\t  (let [channels (:dao.stream.remote/channels opts)\n   725\t        policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n   726\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n   727\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/budget])\n   728\t        links (atom {})]\n   729\t    (fn [descriptor]\n   730\t      (if-not (valid-remote-descriptor? descriptor)\n   731\t        (result :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor)\n   732\t        (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)]\n   733\t          (if-not (contains? channels cd)\n   734\t            (result :dao.stream/not-found)\n   735\t            (do (swap! links\n   736\t                       (fn [m]\n   737\t                         (if (contains? m cd)\n   738\t                           m\n   739\t                           (assoc m cd\n   740\t                                  (new-link (get channels cd) policy)))))\n   741\t                (let [link (get @links cd)\n   742\t                      refl (atom {:link link\n   743\t                                  :descriptor descriptor\n   744\t                                  :identity (:dao.stream/identity\n   745\t                                              descriptor)\n   746\t                                  :surface nil\n   747\t                                  :source-descriptor nil\n   748\t                                  :gone? false\n   749\t                                  :closed? false\n   750\t                                  :ids #{}})]\n   751\t                  (send-request!\n   752\t                    link refl\n   753\t                    (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/descriptor []))\n   754\t                  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   755\t                   :dao.stream/handle (ReflectionHandle. refl)\n   756\t                   :dao.stream/attachment (str (random-uuid))}))))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '1,225p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc | sed -n '1,225p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.remote-test\n     2\t  \"The remote slice: the toy over two in-process ring buffers as the\n     3\t   channel; a gap from an evicting source crossing verbatim with the\n     4\t   source's cursor; blocked then ok on re-ask; not-found marking the\n     5\t   reflection gone while no-surface does not; the descriptor answer\n     6\t   carrying the surface; a kept cursor from a reflection accepted by\n     7\t   the source handle; the budget chase and its terminal non-ok outcome;\n     8\t   oversize; resend-after on an unreliable toy channel; append-unknown\n     9\t   on channel end and at close; refused returned verbatim; close!\n    10\t   semantics; the mirror's four-step order on the wire, its channel\n    11\t   context, and malformed input dropped; the remote descriptor\n    12\t   dispatch; position errors only ever relayed; a send the writer\n    13\t   refuses with full leaving nothing outstanding; and the installed\n    14\t   outcomes kept to their own served stream.\"\n    15\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    16\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    17\t            [dao.stream.middleware :as middleware]\n    18\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n    19\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t;; =============================================================================\n    23\t;; The toy: two in-process ring buffers as the channel\n    24\t;; =============================================================================\n    25\t\n    26\t(defn- ring\n    27\t  \"An open owner ring-buffer handle with the given capacity.\"\n    28\t  [capacity]\n    29\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    30\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/ringbuffer\n    31\t                         :dao.stream.ringbuffer/capacity capacity})))\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t(defn- toy\n    35\t  \"The toy channel: buffer `:ab` carries peer A's values toward peer B,\n    36\t   `:ba` carries B's toward A. Each side's end is {:reader r :writer\n    37\t   w}: A reads ba and writes ab; B's mirror reads ab and writes ba.\"\n    38\t  []\n    39\t  (let [ab (ring 64)\n    40\t        ba (ring 64)\n    41\t        cd {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    42\t            :dao.stream/identity \"toy-channel\"}]\n    43\t    {:channel cd\n    44\t     :ab ab\n    45\t     :ba ba\n    46\t     :a-end {:reader ba :writer ab}\n    47\t     :b-end {:reader ab :writer ba}}))\n    48\t\n    49\t\n    50\t(defn- entry\n    51\t  \"One table entry: the handle and its declared surface.\"\n    52\t  [h surface]\n    53\t  {:handle h :surface surface})\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\t(defn- served-peer\n    57\t  \"Peer B: an atom of the table it serves plus its side of the toy,\n    58\t   with the mirror step's own cursor held in an atom.\"\n    59\t  [table t]\n    60\t  {:table (atom table)\n    61\t   :b-reader (:reader (:b-end t))\n    62\t   :b-writer (:writer (:b-end t))\n    63\t   :mirror (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n    64\t                   (stream/cursor (:reader (:b-end t))\n    65\t                                  :dao.stream/oldest)))})\n    66\t\n    67\t\n    68\t(defn- serve!\n    69\t  \"One mirror step over everything pending on the toy's request\n    70\t   buffer.\"\n    71\t  [peer]\n    72\t  (swap! (:mirror peer)\n    73\t         #(remote/mirror-step @(:table peer) (:b-reader peer)\n    74\t                              % (:b-writer peer))))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn- attach\n    78\t  \"Attach one reflection for `identity` through `end`, a channel end\n    79\t   {:reader r :writer w}, with the attacher's composition data `opts`.\n    80\t   One call builds one attacher, so one call per toy makes one link.\"\n    81\t  [end identity opts]\n    82\t  (let [cd {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    83\t            :dao.stream/identity \"toy-channel\"}\n    84\t        attach! (remote/attacher\n    85\t                  (merge {:dao.stream.remote/channels {cd end}} opts))]\n    86\t    (attach! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n    87\t              :dao.stream/identity identity\n    88\t              :dao.stream/channel cd})))\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\t(defn- values\n    92\t  \"Every retained value of `h`, oldest first, by a fresh cursor walk.\"\n    93\t  [h]\n    94\t  (loop [c (:dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h :dao.stream/oldest))\n    95\t         acc []]\n    96\t    (let [r (stream/next h c)]\n    97\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    98\t        (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) (conj acc (:dao.stream/value r)))\n    99\t        acc))))\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\t(defn- wire-requests\n   103\t  \"The request values currently retained on wire buffer `h`, oldest\n   104\t   first.\"\n   105\t  [h]\n   106\t  (filter #(and (map? %) (contains? % :dao.stream.remote/op))\n   107\t          (values h)))\n   108\t\n   109\t\n   110\t(defn- op-requests\n   111\t  \"The retained requests on wire buffer `h` whose op is `op`. Ring\n   112\t   buffers retain what they carried, so counts of the wire's traffic\n   113\t   are per op.\"\n   114\t  [h op]\n   115\t  (filter #(= op (:dao.stream.remote/op %)) (wire-requests h)))\n   116\t\n   117\t\n   118\t(defn- capped-writer\n   119\t  \"A channel writer that carries values to `h` but refuses, with\n   120\t   invalid-value, any carrying a more vector: the toy's frame budget\n   121\t   stops at one outcome per answer.\"\n   122\t  [h]\n   123\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   124\t    (append!\n   125\t      [_ v]\n   126\t      (if (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/more)\n   127\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value}\n   128\t        (stream/append! h v)))))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn- dropping-writer\n   132\t  \"A channel writer that carries values to `h` but silently drops the\n   133\t   first `n` whose op is one of `ops`, answering ok either way: the\n   134\t   toy's unreliable channel.\"\n   135\t  [h n ops]\n   136\t  (let [left (atom n)]\n   137\t    (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   138\t      (append!\n   139\t        [_ v]\n   140\t        (let [drop? (and (pos? @left)\n   141\t                         (contains? ops (:dao.stream.remote/op v)))]\n   142\t          (when drop? (swap! left dec))\n   143\t          (if drop?\n   144\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}\n   145\t            (stream/append! h v)))))))\n   146\t\n   147\t\n   148\t(defn- full-then-forward-writer\n   149\t  \"A channel writer that refuses, with full, the first `n` appends and\n   150\t   carries every later one to `h`: the toy's back pressure, transient\n   151\t   and then recovered.\"\n   152\t  [h n]\n   153\t  (let [left (atom n)]\n   154\t    (reify stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   155\t      (append!\n   156\t        [_ v]\n   157\t        (if (pos? @left)\n   158\t          (do (swap! left dec)\n   159\t              {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full})\n   160\t          (stream/append! h v))))))\n   161\t\n   162\t\n   163\t(defn- list-stream\n   164\t  \"A minimal served reader over a fixed vector, whose cursors are bare\n   165\t   positions: two of these mint equal cursor values, which two served\n   166\t   identities on one link can hold at once.\"\n   167\t  [identity vs]\n   168\t  (reify stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   169\t\n   170\t    (descriptor\n   171\t      [_]\n   172\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   173\t       :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/list\n   174\t                               :dao.stream/identity identity}\n   175\t       :dao.stream/identity identity})\n   176\t\n   177\t\n   178\t    stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   179\t\n   180\t    (cursor\n   181\t      [_ anchor]\n   182\t      (case anchor\n   183\t        :dao.stream/oldest {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   184\t                            :dao.stream/cursor 0}\n   185\t        :dao.stream/newest {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   186\t                            :dao.stream/cursor (count vs)}\n   187\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-anchor}))\n   188\t\n   189\t    (next\n   190\t      [_ c]\n   191\t      (cond\n   192\t        (not (integer? c))\n   193\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-cursor}\n   194\t\n   195\t        (some? (get vs c))\n   196\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   197\t         :dao.stream/value (get vs c)\n   198\t         :dao.stream/cursor (inc c)}\n   199\t\n   200\t        :else\n   201\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/blocked}))))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t;; =============================================================================\n   205\t;; The proof row\n   206\t;; =============================================================================\n   207\t\n   208\t(deftest the-toy-over-two-ring-buffers\n   209\t  (let [t (toy)\n   210\t        s (ring 8)]\n   211\t    (stream/append! s \"hello\")\n   212\t    (let [peer (served-peer {\"str-1\" (entry s #{:reader})} t)\n   213\t          res (attach (:a-end t) \"str-1\" {})\n   214\t          r (:dao.stream/handle res)]\n   215\t      (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome res)))\n   216\t      (is (some? (:dao.stream/attachment res)))\n   217\t      (testing \"attach sends the descriptor probe, wire-shaped\"\n   218\t        (let [[probe] (wire-requests (:ab t))]\n   219\t          (is (= \"str-1\" (:dao.stream/identity probe)))\n   220\t          (is (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op probe)))\n   221\t          (is (= [] (:dao.stream.remote/args probe)))\n   222\t          (is (contains? probe :dao.stream.remote/id))))\n   223\t      (testing \"descriptor is local: the remote descriptor, the identity\"\n   224\t        (let [d (stream/descriptor r)]\n   225\t          (is (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome d)))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
